            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous heterotopic pregnancy presenting with tubal abortion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1361-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Heterotopic pregnancies are rarely spontaneous. We present the case of a woman who presented with acute abdominal pain. Emergency laparotomy was performed. Intraoperative finding showed right tubal pregnancy and right salpingectomy was performed. Six weeks post-operation, the patient's symptoms and signs of pregnancy persisted and ultrasound showed an intrauterine single viable fetus. The pregnancy was continued to term and a healthy female baby was delivered.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
